/ Signs a Data and verifies, exercises the sign→canonicalize→hash→sign→verify path
/ end-to-end. A clean pass means the typed signing surface is intact. Signing makes a new,
/ signed value (the signature is a layer around the data); `write to` keeps it.
Start
- set %data% = { "message": "round-trip me" }
- sign %data%, write to %signed%
- verify %signed%, write to %verifyResult%
- assert %verifyResult% is true, "signed Data must verify on the same actor"
